[38;2;124;124;124mNote that $k+1$ and $k+2$ are consecutive integers, so one is even and one is [0m
[38;2;124;124;124modd. Thus $v_2(f(k)) = v_2(k+1) + v_2(k+2)$ where exactly one of the two terms [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mis $\geq 1$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mIf $k$ is even: $k+1$ is odd, $k+2$ is even. $v_2(f(k)) = v_2(k+2)$.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mIf $k$ is odd: $k+1$ is even, $k+2$ is odd. $v_2(f(k)) = v_2(k+1)$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo $S = \{v_2(j) : j \geq 2\} = \{0, 1, 2, 3, \ldots\}$ (since $v_2(3) = 0, [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mv_2(2) = 1, v_2(4) = 2$, etc.). Actually $S = \{v_2(j) : j \geq 1\}$ since $k+1$[0m[38;2;124;124;124mranges over $\geq 1$ and $k+2$ ranges over $\geq 2$. So $S = \{0, 1, 2, [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\ldots\}$. Gap is 1, so $m = 1$ works.[0m

